A||N||3||wardog85GT||1000 miles on new clutch and now it won't disengage||||8||
Z||000000||wardog85GT||05-08-2001||09:02 PM||||What gives? I just installed a new clutch, pressure plate and throw out bearing in my 85 GT. I've put about a thousand miles on it with no problems until today. The clutch is not disengaging, and the clutch pedal is very stiff. I checked th slave cylinder and it seems to be working fine. The clutch was a CarQuest factory replacement. Any ideas? I dread having to drop the cradle again.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Bluemagic||05-09-2001||06:11 AM||||Sound like the springs in the clutch disc has collapsed and you have to drop the tranny any way have fun.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-09-2001||06:59 AM||||OR... if you had the old style, welded together clutch fork, it fell apart...like mine did.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||05-09-2001||12:38 PM||||Dropping the tranny is a fairly involved process, so before that avenue is explored I would like to ask you the following...<BR>Did You see if the shaft that protrudes out of the slave cylinder moves about 3/4 to 1 inch when depressed(by having someone press the pedal while you check the shaft)?  If this distance is traveled by the shaft then I am afraid that the clutch hydraulics are working properly and something else has gone awry(tranny removal time).<BR>||||reg||1
